{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-152259","model_call":20,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"gothic rock\" \"lyrical themes\" (+ death religion romanticism nihilism existentialism morbidity))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"gothic rock\" \"lyrical themes\" (+ death religion romanticism nihilism existentialism morbidity))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_30_1437813071#0_3049767224","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2352","rank":1,"snippet":"Contents 1 Musical and lyrical themes 2 History and albums 2.1 Formation 2.2 Slow Deep and Hard and The Origin of the Feces (1991–1992) 2.3 Bloody Kisses and October Rust (1993–1998) 2.4 World Coming Down and The Least Worst of Type O Negative (1999–2001) 2.5 Life Is Killing Me and Dead Again (2002–2009) 2.6 Peter Steele's <cover>death and the end of Type O Negative (2010) 2.7 Additional releases (2011–2018) 3 Trivia 4 Personnel 5 Links to other albums Musical and lyrical themes Many fans describe Type O's music as \"sad, depressed, dark, and haunted\". Type O Negative incorporates mainly gothic metal and doom metal into their music while some sections in certain songs utilize different genres including gothic rock, </cover>psychedelic rock, hard rock, new wave, punk, hardcore punk, thrash metal, sludge metal, and industrial. There are numerous songs that have riffs resembling Black Sabbath, while many nonmetal tones and parts sound like that of The Beatles, The Doors, Pink Floyd, Deep Purple, Led Zeppelin or others. Combining this fact with being a metal band, Black Sabbath has the biggest influence on Type O Negative. The main "},"time":52},"model_calls":20,"document_judgments":16,"relevance_3":3,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
