{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-152259","model_call":49,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"goth rock\" (+ \"deals with\" \"lyrics\" \"lyrical\") (+ alienation despair nihilism death religion sexuality))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"goth rock\" (+ \"deals with\" \"lyrics\" \"lyrical\") (+ alienation despair nihilism death religion sexuality))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_970349970#30_2058894283","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2379","rank":1,"snippet":"80 Doom Metal in the ‘90s Metal concerts are known for being high energy. Best Heavy Metal Bands of the ‘90s #81—100 Gothic Metal in the ‘90s Heavy metal fashion revolves around dark colors. Other Notable Heavy Metal Bands of the ‘90s Groove Metal in the ‘90s \" , \"segment\": \"This style of music combined traditional heavy metal with dark atmospheric gothic rock influences. This form of music evolved out of the death-doom movement, which was a fusion of <cover>death metal and doom metal. This genre stands out for its use of confessional and introspective lyrics, often centered around gothic fiction. This blending of heavy metal and goth rock </cover>can still be heard in the compositions of more symphonic metal bands. Certain gothic metal acts relied on a \"beauty and the beast\" singing style, in which the male vocalist showcases an aggressive singing style while the female vocalist exhibits a clean singing style that's meant as a point of contrast. Classically trained female vocalists became the preferred choice by symphonic metal bands in the 2000s. pinterest-pin-it Heavy metal fashion revolves around dark colors. Wikipedia Commons Other Notable Heavy Metal Bands of "},"time":120},"model_calls":49,"document_judgments":36,"relevance_3":3,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
